{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce targeted tax relief for self-employed taxi and private-hire drivers",
        "additional_details": "Taxi and PHV drivers can face unusually high unavoidable costs just to earn. A driver turning over \u00a340,000 may spend \u00a310,000 on fuel, insurance, licensing, maintenance and vehicle costs, yet existing tax relief only reduces the tax/NI bill by a fraction of that spend. Rental drivers can lose even more to fixed weekly costs. Tax-deductible does not mean reimbursed. We want Government to review this burden and introduce targeted tax relief or allowances so licensed drivers can earn a fairer net income.",
        "background": "Introduce targeted income/NI tax relief for self-employed taxi and PHV drivers. High unavoidable costs mean \u00a340k turnover can leave only ~\u00a325.5k after \u00a310k expenses and taxes. Drivers renting licensed vehicles can face even higher fixed costs.",
